WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.980
He may not have the nostalgic appeal of Tobey&nbsp;
Maguire or the youthful energy of Tom Holland,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.140
but Andrew Garfield still did a great job&nbsp;
bringing Spider-Man to life. So why were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:15.100
"The Amazing Spider-Man" movies canceled after&nbsp;
two movies? And is the series gone for good?

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.640
When Sony made the decision to cancel Sam Raimi's&nbsp;
"Spider-Man 4" and move forward with a reboot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.380
they probably had a grand plan to keep the&nbsp;
franchise going for a while. About a year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.720
after the release of the Andrew Garfield-starring&nbsp;
"Amazing Spider-Man" in 2012, the studio announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.580
an ambitious slate of follow-ups. "The Amazing&nbsp;
Spider-Man 2" had already been greenlit and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:41.940
well underway, but flags were also planted for&nbsp;
two more films to be released in 2016 and 2018.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:47.940
The release of "The Amazing Spider-Man 2" in 2014&nbsp;
didn't meet expectations, though. It was savaged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.920
by critics and earned significantly less than&nbsp;
its predecessor — which itself had already been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:59.460
a steep decline from Raimi's "Spider-Man 3" in&nbsp;
2007. Unsure of how to right the ship, Sony's Amy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:04.740
Pascal made the unprecedented decision to not only&nbsp;
scrap plans for the sequels, but to team up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.561
Marvel Studios and firmly establish Spider-Man&nbsp;
as part of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:09.561 --> 00:01:13.140
This resulted in a complete erasure&nbsp;
of the "Amazing Spider-Man" series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:18.480
halting a third installment and replacing Andrew&nbsp;
Garfield with Tom Holland as Spider-Man. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.080
Garfield may have already been on the&nbsp;
outs — with rumors of his firing even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.340
before the reboot — the series was left off&nbsp;
on something of a cliffhanger for audiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.320
who now had to wonder if they'd ever get closure.&nbsp;
And prior to Garfield's return in "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.880
No Way Home," there unfortunately didn't&nbsp;
seem to be a way forward for a threequel.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.500
"Whatever, I don't know, I&nbsp;
try not to think about it."

00:01:38.668 --> 00:01:40.308
"How's that working out for you?"

00:01:41.193 --> 00:01:42.393
"Perfectly."

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:47.220
Over the years, just about everyone involved&nbsp;
in "The Amazing Spider-Man" and its sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.960
has been asked about a third film. Even after&nbsp;
Marvel Studios transported Andrew Garfield's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.612
version of Peter Parker into the MCU, it's a&nbsp;
question that's been posed to much of the cast.

00:01:56.612 --> 00:01:59.880
Sally Field wasn't thrilled by&nbsp;
the idea — she was apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.332
uninterested in reprising her role&nbsp;
as Aunt May. Field admitted in 2016 —

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:07.360
"It's really hard to find a&nbsp;
three-dimensional character in it."

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.520
Dane DeHaan, who played Harry Osborn, seems&nbsp;
to feel differently. When asked about rumors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.360
of his appearance in "Spider-Man: No&nbsp;
Way Home," the actor told Radio Times —

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.609
"I would certainly love to make&nbsp;
some kind of movie like that again."

00:02:18.609 --> 00:02:23.280
As for Andrew Garfield himself, he's said he'd&nbsp;
happily don the spandex again — but only under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.990
the right circumstances. In 2022, he&nbsp;
told the Happy Sad Confused podcast —

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:32.460
"I am definitely open to that. It would have&nbsp;
to be something very unique, very special,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:36.278
and of service to the audience,&nbsp;
of service to the character."

00:02:36.278 --> 00:02:41.760
In 2016, the MCU introduced a newer, younger Peter&nbsp;
Parker played by Tom Holland in "Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.980
Civil War." An instant fan favorite, it seemed&nbsp;
that audiences had no problem saying goodbye to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:51.360
Andrew Garfield and "The Amazing Spider-Man"&nbsp;
universe. This was further cemented by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.040
enormous success of "Spider-Man: Homecoming"&nbsp;
and "Spider-Man: Far From Home," the latter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.088
which was the first film for the wall-crawler&nbsp;
to pass a billion dollars at the box office.

00:03:00.088 --> 00:03:02.793
But if Garfield thought he&nbsp;
wasn't beloved in the role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.793 --> 00:03:06.060
he must've had a shock when he was asked to&nbsp;
make a surprise appearance in "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.520
No Way Home." Joining forces with both Tom Holland&nbsp;
and Tobey Maguire's versions of the webslinger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.380
Garfield made his triumphant return, and&nbsp;
the fan response was overwhelming. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:21.300
multiple fan petitions popped up on Change.org&nbsp;
encouraging Sony to greenlight "The Amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.860
Spider-Man 3" — including one that&nbsp;
totaled more than 30,000 signatures.

00:03:26.214 --> 00:03:27.654
"I love you guys."

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.071
"Thank you!"

00:03:31.171 --> 00:03:37.020
In 2022, a former Marvel lawyer spoke to Animated&nbsp;
Times and said that — legally speaking — there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.458
was nothing standing in the way of Sony jumping&nbsp;
back into the "Amazing Spider-Man" franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.458 --> 00:03:46.320
But while Sony hasn't commented officially on the&nbsp;
prospect of returning to that series of films, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.160
now seems like a third "Amazing Spider-Man" could&nbsp;
be a real possibility after years of hopelessness.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:56.100
By the end of "The Amazing Spider-Man 2" Gwen&nbsp;
Stacy is dead, leaving Peter Parker to deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.300
with his grief and guilt without her. A scene&nbsp;
near the end of the film teased a host of new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:05.280
villains — and with Dane DeHaan's Green Goblin&nbsp;
now knowing Spider-Man's true identity, it seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:10.560
they were setting up some major new storylines.&nbsp;
Director Marc Webb told Den of Geek in 2017 —

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.000
"We were talking about the Sinister Six. Chris&nbsp;
Cooper was going to come back and play the [Norman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.267
Osborn] Goblin. We were going to freeze his head,&nbsp;
and then he was going to be brought back to life."

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:23.280
Could all of that still happen? Anything&nbsp;
is possible — but with more than 10 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.600
since the film's release, it's just as likely&nbsp;
that something new would be dreamed up. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.267
it was up to Andrew Garfield, it would be&nbsp;
very different from Webb's initial plans.

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:36.060
While speaking with the Happy Sad Confused&nbsp;
podcast, Garfield seemed more excited about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:41.040
notion of facing off with Tom Hardy's anti-hero&nbsp;
Venom. Considering the multiverse shenanigans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.808
introduced in "No Way Home," the possibilities&nbsp;
for a third film are practically endless.

00:04:45.808 --> 00:04:50.160
It might be easy to assume that a third "Amazing&nbsp;
Spider-Man" film would simply bring back the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:55.320
cast of the two previous entries, but that's not&nbsp;
quite as simple as it might sound. For starters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:59.640
Emma Stone probably wouldn't be back — Gwen&nbsp;
Stacy died at the climax of the previous movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:03.480
after all. Plus, with more than a decade&nbsp;
having already passed since "The Amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:07.101
Spider-Man 2," not everyone may&nbsp;
be keen to reprise their roles.

00:05:07.101 --> 00:05:11.820
With several new entries in Sony's own corner&nbsp;
of the Spider-Man universe — including "Venom,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:16.420
"Morbius," and "Kraven the Hunter" — new&nbsp;
opportunities could present themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:19.740
We've already seen the villains Lizard&nbsp;
and Electro make a return in "No Way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:24.660
Home," and they could return as either allies&nbsp;
or enemies as a dangerous threat emerges. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.460
are plenty more characters to choose from:&nbsp;
Tom Hardy's Venom, Michael Keaton's Vulture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:33.401
B.J. Novak's Alistair Smythe,&nbsp;
or even Paul Giamatti's Rhino.

00:05:33.401 --> 00:05:37.857
"On behalf of the fine people of New&nbsp;
York City and real rhinos everywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.857 --> 00:05:40.735
I ask you to put your mechanized paws in the air."

00:05:40.735 --> 00:05:41.781
"Never!"

00:05:41.781 --> 00:05:46.200
Another route might be for a sequel to feature an&nbsp;
all-new supporting cast as Spider-Man faces off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:50.640
against an entirely new enemy that we've yet&nbsp;
to see on screen. This might be the smartest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:55.920
way to go, in order to help the series separate&nbsp;
itself from its previous lackluster installments.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.600
To say that the first two "Amazing Spider-Man"&nbsp;
films were divisive among fans and critics would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:04.500
be something of an understatement. While&nbsp;
Andrew Garfield, Emma Stone, and the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.520
of the films' casts were largely praised for&nbsp;
their performances, both movies were met with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:13.260
criticism from reviewers for their half-baked,&nbsp;
overly complicated plots. Some even felt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:17.640
the creators of the films didn't even understand&nbsp;
the character of Spider-Man, with their grim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.022
dark takes on the source material not gelling&nbsp;
with many long-time fans of the comics.

00:06:22.022 --> 00:06:25.020
The overwhelming fan response to&nbsp;
Garfield's return in "No Way Home"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.080
proves there's a clear appetite for&nbsp;
more stories set in that universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.120
though — and a third film would be an opportunity&nbsp;
for Sony to finally do it right. It would also be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.600
their chance to prove that they can make a&nbsp;
great live-action "Spider-Man" film on their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:40.920
own — without Sam Raimi or Marvel Studios&nbsp;
— the same way they did in animation with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.460
"Into the Spider-Verse." A new story&nbsp;
could also fix mistakes of the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:49.420
such as the death of Gwen Stacy or the awkward&nbsp;
new interpretation of the Green Goblin.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.920
With the introduction of the multiverse,&nbsp;
for example, we could meet a Gwen Stacy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:58.080
from another reality — maybe even a live-action&nbsp;
Spider-Gwen. Not only would this allow Emma Stone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.580
to reappear against all odds, but it would&nbsp;
also provide a tangible way for Garfield's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.200
version of Peter Parker to come face to face&nbsp;
with the grief and pain caused by her death.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.500
During "Spider-Man: No Way Home," we&nbsp;
learn that the past several years have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.400
been pretty hard on Andrew Garfield's&nbsp;
Peter Parker. After losing Gwen Stacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.180
Peter was unable to forgive himself — and&nbsp;
while he tried to keep on being a friendly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.281
neighborhood hero, he actually turned&nbsp;
into a much darker, angrier character.

00:07:22.281 --> 00:07:25.701
"At some point, I just… I&nbsp;
stopped pulling my punches.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.702 --> 00:07:30.902
I got rageful."

00:07:30.902 --> 00:07:35.340
Thankfully, the events of "No Way Home" help&nbsp;
Garfield's traumatized hero to heal — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:38.580
the actor believes his character will be&nbsp;
very different the next time we see him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.822 --> 00:07:43.442
In the official art book for "No Way Home,"&nbsp;
Garfield elaborates a bit on this, saying —

00:07:43.442 --> 00:07:46.440
"He's going back knowing that he&nbsp;
has brothers. He's going back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:51.600
re-inspired to follow his destiny, his calling&nbsp;
— the purpose of his life. By catching MJ,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:55.364
he got to make up for a terrible tragedy&nbsp;
that he tried to avoid in his world."

00:07:55.364 --> 00:07:57.780
Garfield also believes that&nbsp;
Peter had his eyes opened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:00.404
to the mysteries of the multiverse, explaining —

00:08:00.404 --> 00:08:04.500
"I think he's going back with a mind blown&nbsp;
about the cosmos and the universe and string&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:09.216
theory and multiple dimensionality. He's&nbsp;
going back incredibly reinvigorated."

00:08:09.216 --> 00:08:12.336
If we ever get to see this version&nbsp;
of Peter back in his own world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.336 --> 00:08:15.480
he probably won't be hitting the&nbsp;
bad guys quite as hard — and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:19.440
might be trying to dig deeper into the&nbsp;
multiverse, for better or for worse.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.460
Considering that Marvel Studios is moving&nbsp;
full steam ahead on more films in their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:27.720
"Spider-Man" series starring Tom Holland, one&nbsp;
might wonder how they'd react to Sony embarking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:32.100
on a separate journey with a wallcrawler from the&nbsp;
past. Back when the deal to bring Spider-Man into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:37.592
the MCU was first being struck, Marvel's Kevin&nbsp;
Feige had no interest in continuing the series.

00:08:37.592 --> 00:08:43.140
Sony head honcho Amy Pascal had apparently always&nbsp;
intended for "Amazing Spider-Man 3" to follow the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:48.540
deal with Marvel Studios, just with more direct&nbsp;
input from them to ensure a success. It was Feige&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:53.289
who forced Sony's hand to reboot the franchise&nbsp;
rather than bring Andrew Garfield into the fold.

00:08:53.289 --> 00:08:56.760
Today, given Marvel's success with the&nbsp;
multiverse — where variants of the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:01.200
character can co-exist with audiences clearly&nbsp;
appreciating multiple stories living side by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.280
side — Feige and Marvel may not be as&nbsp;
opposed as you might think. At least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:10.693
not if you ask Holland, who clearly has no room&nbsp;
for jealousy. The actor told Comicbook.com —

00:09:10.693 --> 00:09:14.820
"I would love to see 'The Amazing Spider-Man&nbsp;
3.' I think what was so wonderful was how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:18.120
Andrew [Garfield] was able to kind of make&nbsp;
amends with the character and the studio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:22.380
you know, to kind of win the general public&nbsp;
back. [...] So should Sony decide to do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:26.045
they would have my full support,&nbsp;
and obviously, so would Andrew."

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.240
"Who are you?"

00:09:29.707 --> 00:09:31.127
"I'm Spider-Man."

